.Dd May 25, 2026
.Dt XTC_STRERROR 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_strerror
.Nd return a stable English description of an xtc error code
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.Ft const char *
.Fn xtc_strerror "int xtc_err"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn xtc_strerror
function returns a stable English description of the xtc error code
.Fa xtc_err .
.Pp
Recognised values are
.Dv XTC_OK
and the
.Dv XTC_E_*
codes declared in
.In xtc.h .
For any code outside the recognised set the function returns the
string
.Dq unknown ;
it never returns
.Dv NULL .
.Pp
The returned pointer is to static storage and must not be freed.
The exact text for each known code is part of the API contract for
log-message stability and changes only on a major version bump.
.Pp
The codes, their values, and the text each one reads as:
.Bl -column "XTC_E_RESOURCE" "-12" -offset indent
.It Sy Code Ta Sy Value Ta Sy Text
.It Dv XTC_OK Ta 0 Ta Dq ok
.It Dv XTC_E_INVAL Ta \-1 Ta Dq invalid argument
.It Dv XTC_E_NOMEM Ta \-2 Ta Dq out of memory
.It Dv XTC_E_NOSYS Ta \-3 Ta Dq not implemented on this platform
.It Dv XTC_E_RANGE Ta \-4 Ta Dq numeric out of range
.It Dv XTC_E_AGAIN Ta \-5 Ta Dq resource temporarily unavailable
.It Dv XTC_E_INTERNAL Ta \-6 Ta Dq internal invariant violation
.It Dv XTC_E_RESOURCE Ta \-7 Ta Dq resource cap reached
.It Dv XTC_E_DEADLK Ta \-8 Ta Dq deadlock victim
.It Dv XTC_E_VERSION Ta \-9 Ta Dq version mismatch
.It Dv XTC_E_ABORTED Ta \-10 Ta Dq operation aborted
.It Dv XTC_E_NOTFOUND Ta \-11 Ta Dq requested item does not exist
.It Dv XTC_E_IO Ta \-12 Ta Dq I/O error
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
A non-NULL pointer to a NUL-terminated string.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <stdio.h>
#include <xtc.h>

void log_rc(int rc) {
        if (rc != XTC_OK)
                fprintf(stderr, "xtc error: %s\en", xtc_strerror(rc));
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc 7 ,
.Xr xtc_version_string 3
.Sh HISTORY
First appeared in xtc 0.0.1.
